  <header>
    <h1>Privacy Policy — Block Puzzle Master</h1>
    <div class="eff">Effective: 28 September 2026</div>
  </header>

  <h2>1. Overview</h2>
  <p>Block Puzzle Master ("the app," "we," "us") is a block-placement puzzle game. This policy applies to the app across Classic, Daily Challenge, and Adventure modes, and to the version distributed on Google Play (and any other store we later publish to).</p>
  <p>In short: the app doesn't ask you to create an account, doesn't collect your name, email, or any personal information, and doesn't access your contacts, camera, microphone, or location. Your scores, coins, and progress are saved only on your own device. The app contains <strong>no real-money purchases</strong>. Two Google services are used behind the scenes: Google AdMob to show ads (Section 4), and Google Firebase to deliver optional reminder notifications and remotely tune non-personal in-app content (Section 5). The app also uses Google Play to check for and install app updates (Section 6).</p>

  <h2>2. Information we don't collect</h2>
  <p>The app has no login and no chat or social features. Specifically, we never ask for or access:</p>
  <div class="lists">
    <div class="box"><h4>Not collected by the app</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><span class="x">✕</span> Name, email address, or phone number</li>
        <li><span class="x">✕</span> Precise or coarse location</li>
        <li><span class="x">✕</span> Camera, microphone, or photo library</li>
        <li><span class="x">✕</span> Contacts or other apps on your device</li>
        <li><span class="x">✕</span> Payment or financial information</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="box"><h4>Stored, but only on your device</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> High score &amp; games played</li>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> Sound / music preferences</li>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> Daily Challenge &amp; Adventure progress</li>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> Coins &amp; boosters (virtual, in-game only)</li>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> Your in-progress game, so you can resume it</li>
        <li><span class="y">✓</span> Your reminder-notification on/off choice</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p><strong>No real-money purchases.</strong> Coins are a free, virtual in-game currency earned through play; buying boosters spends coins, not money, so no payment or financial information is ever requested or processed.</p>
  <div class="callout">The one exception, described fully in Section 5: if you turn reminder notifications on, Google Firebase generates an anonymous device messaging token so it can deliver them. That token identifies your device installation for message delivery only — it is not your name, email, or any other personal identifier, and we never see or store it ourselves.</div>

  <h2>3. Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>To remember your progress and preferences between sessions, the app keeps a small local database on your device (using an on-device storage library called Hive). This data is never uploaded to a server we operate, and we have no way to see it. It contains:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your high score and total games played</li>
    <li>Total lines cleared, best combo streak, and highest single-move score, used for lifetime stats and Daily Challenge / Adventure objective tracking</li>
    <li>Sound and music on/off preferences</li>
    <li>Daily Challenge completion streak and last-played date</li>
    <li>Adventure Mode level progress, and your <strong>Adventure star ratings (0–3 per level)</strong> and reward progress</li>
    <li>Your <strong>coin balance and booster inventory</strong> — a virtual, in-game currency and items earned by playing or bought with coins (never with real money)</li>
    <li>A snapshot of any game you exit mid-session, so you can pick up where you left off (Resume Game)</li>
    <li>Whether you've already used your one free Extra Life for the current run</li>
    <li>Whether you've turned reminder notifications on, whether you've already seen the one-time notification permission prompt, and the last date you were shown the optional "update available" prompt</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This information stays on your device for as long as the app is installed. Uninstalling the app, or clearing its storage in your device's Settings → Apps → Block Puzzle Master → Storage, permanently deletes it. We cannot recover it for you, because we never had a copy.</p>

  <h2>4. Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
  <p>The app is supported by ads served through Google AdMob (the Google Mobile Ads SDK), in three places:</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Ad type</th><th>When it appears</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Banner</td><td>A small, fixed ad strip at the bottom of the Home and Play screens.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Interstitial</td><td>A full-screen ad shown occasionally when you return to the Home screen from a game.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Rewarded</td><td>Optional. Only shown when you choose to watch a short video in exchange for a reward — for example an Extra Life after a Game Over, extra Adventure Energy, an Adventure booster, or doubling the coins you just earned. You always decide whether to watch; a rewarded ad is never shown automatically.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>To select, serve, and measure these ads, Google and its advertising partners may process technical and advertising data such as your device's advertising identifier, IP address, general device information, approximate location inferred from IP address, and how you interact with an ad. This processing is carried out by Google as described in Google's own policies, not by us directly:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.google.com/about/company/user-consent-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's EU User Consent Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How AdMob uses data</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ads may be delivered through Google AdMob <strong>mediation</strong>, which can route ad requests to third-party ad networks (currently <strong>InMobi</strong>). Those partners process ad-related technical/advertising data under their own privacy policies, alongside Google — see <a href="https://www.inmobi.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">InMobi's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p class="mut">Internet access is requested by the app so ads can load and so the notification/config/update features in Sections 5–6 can work — gameplay itself works fully offline.</p>

  <h2>5. Notifications &amp; Firebase</h2>
  <p>The app uses Google Firebase for two things, both unrelated to advertising: optional reminder notifications, and remotely adjusting a small number of non-personal in-app values (for example, the text shown in a reminder, or the version label and notes shown in the "update available" prompt).</p>
  <h3>Reminder notifications</h3>
  <p>You can turn on optional daily reminders from the in-app Settings menu — a Daily Challenge reminder each morning and a game reminder each evening. This is off by default and entirely your choice; the app asks Android for notification permission only if and when you turn this on.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Most reminders are scheduled locally on your device (via the device's own OS notification scheduler), and re-registered after a restart so they still fire on time.</li>
    <li>If your device also supports it, the app registers with Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) so reminder content can be delivered or refreshed as a push message. This assigns your device installation an anonymous messaging token, generated and held by Google/Firebase — see the callout in Section 2.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Remote configuration</h3>
  <p>Firebase Remote Config lets us adjust small, non-personal values already built into the app (like reminder wording, or the update prompt's version label and notes) without shipping an app update. It does not collect personal information; Google processes standard app-instance/technical data to serve the configuration, similar in nature to the technical data described in Section 4.</p>
  <p>You can turn reminders off at any time from in-app Settings, or deny/revoke the notification permission from your device's own Settings → Apps → Block Puzzle Master → Notifications — either way, no further reminders are scheduled or delivered. See <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firebase's privacy &amp; security information</a> for how Google handles this data.</p>

  <h2>6. App updates (Google Play)</h2>
  <p>On start-up the app asks <strong>Google Play</strong> whether a newer version is available and, if you choose to update, downloads and installs it through Google Play's own in-app update service. This uses standard Google Play technical/app data and involves <strong>no personal information</strong>; it works only on installs from Google Play. If an update is available you can always choose "Later" — the app never updates without your action.</p>

  <h2>7. App permissions</h2>
  <p>Block Puzzle Master requests the following Android permissions:</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Permission</th><th>Why it's needed</th></tr>
    <tr><td>INTERNET</td><td>Required to request/display ads (AdMob), to send/receive reminder notifications and remote configuration (Firebase), and to check for/download app updates (Google Play).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</td><td>Lets the app check whether a network connection is available before requesting an ad or a Firebase/Play update, rather than failing silently.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST_NOTIFICATIONS</td><td>Required by Android to show any notification at all. Only requested at the moment you turn reminders on in Settings — never at first launch.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED</td><td>Lets the app re-register your already-scheduled reminders after your device restarts (Android clears scheduled alarms on reboot otherwise). Used only if you've turned reminders on; does not run the full app in the background.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>No other permission — location, camera, microphone, contacts, or storage — is requested at install or run time.</p>

  <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>Block Puzzle Master does not knowingly collect personal information from children. The app itself collects no personal information from any player, of any age, as described in Section 2. Reminder notifications (Section 5) are opt-in and are never personalized based on anything other than the time of day.</p>
  <p>Because the app shows ads via Google AdMob, if you believe this app may be used by, or directed at, children under 13 (or the relevant age of consent in your region), we configure AdMob's ad requests accordingly (for example, requesting non-personalized ads and applying Google's child-directed treatment / ad content filtering settings) so that ad serving complies with COPPA and similar regulations.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Note for the developer:</strong> confirm the app's intended audience in Google Play Console's target-audience declaration, and set AdMob's "Tag for child-directed treatment" / "Tag for users under the age of consent" to match before publishing.</div>

  <h2>9. Data sharing &amp; sale</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal data — we don't collect any to begin with. We do not operate any server that stores player accounts, scores, coins, or gameplay data. The only outside party involved in the app is Google, acting as an independent service provider for three separate purposes: advertising via AdMob and its mediation partners (Section 4), reminder delivery / remote configuration via Firebase (Section 5), and app-update delivery via Google Play (Section 6).</p>

  <h2>10. Data security</h2>
  <p>Because your progress is stored only on your device rather than transmitted to servers we control, its protection depends on your device's own security (screen lock, OS-level app sandboxing, and encryption where your device provides it). We do not operate a server-side database of player information ourselves. If you enable reminder notifications, Google/Firebase's own infrastructure briefly holds a device messaging token to deliver them — governed by Google's security practices, not ours.</p>

  <h2>11. Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Clear your local data</strong> — uninstall the app, or go to Settings → Apps → Block Puzzle Master → Storage → Clear storage on your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Turn sound or music off</strong> — from the in-app Settings menu; this preference is saved locally.</li>
    <li><strong>Turn reminder notifications off</strong> — from the in-app Settings menu, or by revoking notification permission in your device's Settings → Apps → Block Puzzle Master → Notifications.</li>
    <li><strong>Opt out of personalized ads</strong> — on Android, go to Settings → Google → Ads and turn on "Opt out of Ads Personalization," or reset your advertising ID from the same screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Requests about data Google processes</strong> — because that processing (AdMob, Firebase, and Google Play alike) is Google's, not ours, requests to access or delete it are handled through Google's own privacy controls.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>12. International users</h2>
  <p>The app is available globally. Because AdMob, Firebase, and Google Play all operate global infrastructure, the limited technical, advertising, and messaging data described in Sections 4–6 may be processed in countries other than the one you're playing in, under Google's own cross-border safeguards.</p>

  <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes — for example, if a new feature changes what data is involved — we'll update this page and change the "Effective" date at the top. We encourage checking back occasionally. Continued use of the app after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

